#      ties to the lower column, the selected columns in ascending order, -1 fill; decode rows on a cluster of up to 16
#      CTAs each (slice histograms combined through distributed shared memory). Bit-exact against a torch reference on
#      1215 cases (bf16-valued, tied, -inf-masked, NaN / +-0 rows, short rows, strided outputs, prefill and decode row
#      forms, every cluster size, up to 512K columns), identical over 30 runs and from a CUDA graph. 6 rows, bf16-valued:
#      4K columns 4.9 us vs persistent_topk 7.4, 32K 7.8 vs 15.5, 131K 9.4 vs 15.1, 300K 12.7 vs 15.8, 512K 20.5 vs 29.4
#      (faster at every width 1K-512K); prefill (long rows read twice) 4096 x 2K 28 vs 21 us, x 32K 174 vs 153 (tied rows
#      29 vs 288 and 206 vs 403). Built in but OFF by default
#      (it changes which tied positions the indexer keeps): VLLM_MOET_DET_TOPK=1 at runtime turns it on.
#  27. The decode MoE of b12x's compact W4A8 micro path in one persistent kernel (patch_flashinfer_b12x_moe_fused_sm120.py
#      + b12x_moe_fused/): FC1 (gate/up projection) -> SwiGLU + MXFP8 activation -> FC2 (down projection) from one grid,
#      with the same bits as b12x's three kernels (and step 22's FC2) in projections, intermediate and route_output; b12x's
#      rows-quant before and TopKSum after stay. FC1 items (expert x 10 tiles, one stream per SM, 8-stage cp.async ring +
#      L2 prefetch) then FC2 items (expert x 160 64-column blocks, double-buffered) in the order the experts become ready;
#      the CTA finishing a K128 slice's second tile activates the slice; the last CTA resets the control block (graph
#      replay). On 160 recorded C1 routings (22.5 distinct experts) 65.9 us vs projection 41.9 + activation 1.8 + grouped
#      FC2 23.8; the served MoE path in a CUDA graph 73.2 vs 75.7 us per layer (two nodes fewer): about -100 us per C1
#      decode step; 36 distinct experts 95.4 vs 99.5 us. Slower with few distinct experts (6 / 12: +4 / +3 us), so the
#      kernel asks for >= 32 pairs per launch (the drafter's MoE stays on b12x). Built in but OFF by default:
#      VLLM_MOET_B12X_MOE_FUSED=1 at runtime turns it on.
#  28. The DeepSeek-V4.1 sparse MLA decode with its candidate rows gathered by plain loads, the fp4 -> fp8 conversion
#      shared by the two producer groups, the first tile's index words loaded before the candidate lengths, the softmax /
#      P-quantization / XV section with 4 barriers per tile instead of 20, and a merge whose loads are issued up front
#      (patch_flashinfer_sparse_mla_ldg_sm120.py + sparse_mla_ldg/): FlashInfer's own decode kernel text, copied from
#      the installed header at build time (gen_spec_kernel.py: two insertions and one block replacement, each verified
#      against the header; the replaced block pinned by hash), compiled with FlashInfer's flags and instantiated with a
#      gather schedule whose 128 threads load the 32 rows of a tile as 16-byte words (one DRAM round trip) instead of
#      the gather warp's 32-64 cp.async.bulk copies the TMA unit works off one by one (~2.5 us per tile), then convert
#      their half of the tile while the next tile's index is in flight. The restructured section keeps every expression
#      and its order (values the original passed through shared memory pass through an empty asm) and quantizes the P x
#      V-scale operand of all 16 scale groups before one barrier instead of one group per step; each step owns its
#      accumulator, so the sums are unchanged. Output, LSE and the split scratch keep their bits (175 random mixed-cache
#      shapes, partial lists, graph replay). The merge kernel is FlashInfer's expression by expression with the partial
#      rows and the attention sink loaded before the LSE reductions. Served C1 shape (6 tokens, 128 SWA + 512 compressed
#      candidates, 10 splits, cold L2, CUDA graph): decode 10.5 -> 7.5 us, merge 2.6-2.9 -> 2.1 us per layer (r13's first
#      round: 8.2 / 2.1; pb-deep: decode 10.08 -> 8.75 us, critical path -50 us per step). Built in but OFF by default:
#      VLLM_MOET_SPARSE_MLA_LDG=1 at runtime turns it on (VLLM_MOET_SPARSE_MLA_LDG_MERGE=0 keeps FlashInfer's merge);
#      SWA-only layers, prefill and NVFP4 plans stay on FlashInfer's execute.
#  29. GEMV v3 units per round: every R now launched with PDL + evict-first (before, R = 2 / 4 ran without both) and a
#      per-shape table (sm120_gemv/mxfp8_gemv_sm120.cu, in step 3's extension) that keeps R = 1 everywhere: in a graph of
#      back-to-back GEMVs R = 2 / 4 won on two shapes (7.13 -> 6.54, 4.96 -> 3.79 us, same bits for every R), in the served
#      decode graph they lost (critical path +27 us per step). VLLM_MOET_GEMV_V3_R=1|2|4 forces one R (0 = table).
#  30. The DSpark / DFlash drafter's input preparation in one launch for all draft KV-cache groups
#      (patch_vllm_dflash_prepare_groups_sm120.py): the original Triton kernel with the per-group part (context / query
#      slot mappings, their padding) instantiated for up to three groups, the shared outputs written once by the same
#      expressions - every buffer bit-identical (96 random cases incl. padded tails); 3 launches x 9.4 us outside the
#      graphs per decode step -> one: eager 45.2 -> 18.6 us per step. OFF by default: VLLM_MOET_DFLASH_PREP_GROUPS=1.
#  31. The DSA candidate-block selection on the deterministic top-k (patch_vllm_candidate_short_sm120.py): the
#      candidate-source indexer (layer 20) picks its top 2048 blocks of 8 positions per decode row through torch.topk
#      over the static max_model_len-wide score row (no DeepSelect on sm_120): ~20 launches, ~45 us per step on the
#      critical path, inside the FULL decode graph. torch.topk's set - the k largest, equal values to the lower index,
#      NaN above +inf - is what step 26's det_topk kernel computes on [0, valid blocks) of the score row (one cluster
#      launch per row count: graph-safe for every context length); a small kernel then applies the original's -inf ->
#      -1 rule to the selected blocks. 72 random cases incl. long contexts with ties straddling the k-th place: the
#      same sets and bit-identical logits after apply_candidate_mask; served shape in a graph 41.3 -> 3.2 us (2.7K
#      context) / 39.8 -> 10.2 us (60K). OFF by default: VLLM_MOET_CANDIDATE_DET_TOPK=1.
#  32. Each SWA metadata builder's decode build in one launch (patch_vllm_swa_decode_build_sm120.py): the eight
#      builders of the target model ran torch.ge(slot_mapping, 0), a fill of the lens tail and
#      _compute_swa_indices_and_lens_kernel per decode step outside the graphs (24 launches); one kernel per builder
#      now computes the validity from the slot mapping, stores it, runs the original row body unchanged and zeroes the
#      lens tail - every byte the three operations wrote, with the same value (96 random cases). Eight builders at
#      the served step, eager: 175.9 -> 100.3 us. OFF by default: VLLM_MOET_SWA_DECODE_BUILD=1.
#  33. The shared-expert add fused into b12x's top-k sum (patch_vllm_moe_topksum_add_sm120.py): every MoE layer ended
#      with W4A16TopKSumKernel (fp32 adds of the token's routed rows in route order, one bf16 rounding) followed by
#      vLLM's shared_output + fused_output (bf16(float(a) + float(b))): 40 adds of 1.2 us and 40 graph nodes per step
#      on the critical path. One Triton launch computes the same sum (unrouted entries add +0.0 through the load mask:
#      acc is never -0.0, so the value is the same), rounds it to bf16 as the kernel did and adds the shared row as
#      torch did; the runner publishes the layer's shared-experts helper, the fused launch waits on its aux-stream
#      event where the runner would have, and the runner skips its add. 48 random cases bit-identical; served shape
#      in a graph 1.80 -> 1.03 us per layer. OFF by default: VLLM_MOET_MOE_TOPKSUM_ADD=1.
#  34. The decode MoE's rows quantization off the critical path (patch_vllm_moe_prequant_sm120.py): b12x's prepared
#      MXFP8 rows quantize ran on the main stream between the router's top-k and the fused MoE kernel (1.2 us + a gap
#      per layer) although it depends on neither; the runner now launches the same kernel on a side stream before
#      select_experts into vllm-moet-owned buffers of the scratch layout, and the compact-micro launcher hands those
#      to the fused MoE after joining the side stream (same kernel, same input, same bytes; any mismatch quantizes as
#      before). pb-deep C1 (r18, det switches): greedy outputs of six prompts identical with and without, the quant's
#      27.6 us per step leave the critical path, period 9,885 -> 9,803 us. OFF by default: VLLM_MOET_MOE_PREQUANT=1.
#  35. The router's spread GEMM and DeepSeek-V4's routing top-6 in one launch (bf16_gemm/bf16_replica_gemm_sm120.cu
#      spread_topk_kernel + dsv4_topk_sm120.py): replica_mm keeps the router GEMM pending and the top-k takes it;
#      the tile reducers compute the routing scores of their columns, the CTA finishing the last tile selects the
#      top-6 (two rows per warp, interleaved) - GEMM and top-k arithmetic unchanged, 96 random cases bit-identical,
#      pb-deep greedy outputs identical. Measured and NOT worth it: isolated 6.45 vs 6.56 us (PDL), in the served
#      graph 10.7 us vs spread 6.6 + top-k 3.9 - the serial selection tail costs what the top-k launch cost; the
#      critical path did not move (8,271 -> 8,260 us). OFF by default (VLLM_MOET_ROUTER_TOPK_FUSED=1); kept for the
#      MoE-sublayer megakernel, where the routing phase runs on all CTAs.
#  36. The DSpark drafter's non-causal SWA metadata update in one launch (patch_vllm_swa_draft_build_sm120.py):
#      update_draft_decode_metadata() ran, per SWA builder of the drafter (three) inside the drafter's graph,
#      torch.ge(slot_mapping, 0), the token -> request binary search and the non-causal indices kernel - nine launches
#      of 0.9-1.6 us per step. One Triton launch per builder computes the token's validity and request index (the same
#      comparison, the same binary search) and runs the non-causal kernel's row body unchanged; tail programs write the
#      validity past the draft tokens. Bit-identical by construction and by test. OFF by default: VLLM_MOET_SWA_DRAFT_BUILD=1.
#  Since the -pdl tag the kernels of steps 3, 8, 10 and 11 also launch with programmatic dependent launch where it
#  pays - the dense / grouped MXFP8 GEMVs (VLLM_MOET_GEMV_PDL, plus VLLM_MOET_GEMV_EVICT_FIRST for v3's weights), the
#  MoE router (VLLM_MOET_BF16_GEMM_PDL, default router), moe_quant_scatter (VLLM_MOET_MOE_QUANT_SCATTER_PDL); the mHC
#  boundary kernel's PDL variant (VLLM_MOET_MHC_PDL) reads only its norm weight before griddepcontrol.wait - and the
#  indexer's one-slice chain has an opt-in ring variant (VLLM_MOET_BF16_CHAIN=v2). All bit-identical; =0 restores
#  the plain launches.
#  Every vLLM-file step has a build-arg (=0 leaves it out) so a step whose patcher does not fit a newer vLLM yet
#  can be built around: VLLM_MOET_REASONING_EFFORT (4), VLLM_MOET_NVFP4_KV (2's indexer gate + 5),
#  VLLM_MOET_OFFLOAD_DEDUP (6), VLLM_MOET_MHC_OVERLAP (10; VLLM_MOET_DSPARK_MHC_STREAM for the drafter's stream alone),
#  VLLM_MOET_BF16_GEMM (11), VLLM_MOET_ENGRAM_WKV_TP (12), VLLM_MOET_NCCL_GRAPH_RECORDS (13), VLLM_MOET_MOE_FC2_DISCARD (14),
#  VLLM_MOET_PREFILL_DBO (15, default 0 on this base), VLLM_MOET_INDEXER_SHARD_ROWS (16), VLLM_MOET_B12X_COMPACT_BIND (17),
#  VLLM_MOET_DRAFTER_LM_HEAD_MXFP8 (18), VLLM_MOET_DSV4_TOPK (19), VLLM_MOET_FUSED_MARKOV (20),
#  VLLM_MOET_TARGET_LM_HEAD_MXFP8_PATCH (21), VLLM_MOET_B12X_FC2_GROUPED (22), VLLM_MOET_DET_TOPK_PATCH (26),
#  VLLM_MOET_B12X_MOE_FUSED_PATCH (27), VLLM_MOET_SPARSE_MLA_LDG_PATCH (28), VLLM_MOET_DFLASH_PREP_GROUPS_PATCH (30),
#  VLLM_MOET_CANDIDATE_DET_TOPK_PATCH (31), VLLM_MOET_SWA_DECODE_BUILD_PATCH (32), VLLM_MOET_MOE_TOPKSUM_ADD_PATCH (33),
#  VLLM_MOET_MOE_PREQUANT_PATCH (34), VLLM_MOET_SWA_DRAFT_BUILD_PATCH (36).
#
# Build (repo root):
#   DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 docker build -f Dockerfile.sm120-dsv41-nightly -t vllm-moet-sm120:dsv41-nightly-df3bd094-<tag> .
#   The 21d93d0d images came from this file at 59a0136 (base vllm-openai:nightly-21d93d0d + FlashInfer 0.7.1rc2 installed
#   over the base's 0.7.0.post1 + DeepGEMM e1f418c2): -pdl (steps 1-14, served since 2026-10-13 16:27Z, window 8) and
#   -side (6aafbb6, window 9 on 2026-10-14, not kept, see the port doc). The images on vllm-openai:nightly 0961bbae with
#   FlashInfer 0.7.0.dev20260922 came from it before that: -pdl at c066be9, -engram (steps 1-12) at f7cc6d9, and with
#   fewer steps -bf16, -mhc, -moeqs, -ced, -kvdedup and dsv41-nightly-20260923 (git log).
# Serve: docker/sm120/run-dsv41.sh with IMAGE=vllm-moet-sm120:dsv41-nightly-df3bd094-<tag> KV_MODE=upstream
#   (KV_RECORD=nvfp4 -> --kv-cache-dtype nvfp4_ds_mla, fp8_ds_mla -> --kv-cache-dtype fp8_ds_mla). A new FlashInfer
#   version starts with an empty FlashInfer autotune cache (vLLM keys it by FlashInfer's version / arch dir): the
#   first start autotunes again (GPU_MEM_UTIL 0.92 for that start, as for any empty autotune cache).
# Validation: docs/dsv41-sm120-port.md; op-level tests: tools/dsv41_sm120/README.md.

ARG BASE_IMAGE=vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-df3bd094aeea829f27baa0a5282830464f601d9f@sha256:b91d90a63b75d00e780287e4236123a281ee3d29122c864a7044a19a680fdf9d

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- deep_gemm
FROM ${BASE_IMAGE} AS deepgemm-builder
# vLLM's pin (cmake/external_projects/deepgemm.cmake / tools/install_deepgemm.sh): the vllm-project fork of
# DeepGEMM, 727f8470 (one commit after a7a92773 of vllm#61744 - upstream 2.8.1 + the SM120 port, on torch's stable
# ABI - writing FP8 einsum output scale factors in the 128x4 tiled layout); needs the cutlass and deep_jit submodules.
ARG DEEPGEMM_REPO=https://github.com/vllm-project/DeepGEMM.git
ARG DEEPGEMM_REF=727f847082d2e7946f70dc02b94949db206310d3
# libdw-dev: deep_jit's exception.hpp includes elfutils/libdwfl.h (compile-time only; the
# vendored _C_extension links neither libdw nor libelf).
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends git libdw-dev \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir --break-system-packages pybind11 wheel
RUN git clone "$DEEPGEMM_REPO" /deepgemm \
    && cd /deepgemm && git checkout "$DEEPGEMM_REF" \
    && git submodule update --init --depth 1 third-party/cutlass third-party/deep_jit
COPY tools/dsv41_sm120/patch_deepgemm.py /tmp/patch_deepgemm.py
RUN python3 /tmp/patch_deepgemm.py /deepgemm
RUN mkdir -p /tmp/linklibs \
    && ln -sf /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/nvidia/cu13/lib/libnvrtc.so.13 /tmp/linklibs/libnvrtc.so \
    && ln -sf /usr/local/cuda/lib64/libcudart.so.13 /tmp/linklibs/libcudart.so \
    && cd /deepgemm \
    && CPATH=/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/nvidia/cu13/include \
       LIBRARY_PATH=/tmp/linklibs \
       python3 setup.py build_ext --inplace \
    && ls -la /deepgemm/deep_gemm/_C_extension.abi3.so

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- final image
FROM ${BASE_IMAGE}

# 1. DeepGEMM _C_extension with the SM120 128-row paged MQA path and the SM120 per-group BLOCK_M (the vendored
#    Python and JIT device sources are the same commit, so they stay as shipped).
COPY --from=deepgemm-builder /deepgemm/deep_gemm/_C_extension.abi3.so \
     /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/third_party/deep_gemm/_C_extension.abi3.so

# 2. The base's FlashInfer must carry flashinfer#5197 (the DSv4.1 dual cache) and the sm120f AOT modules; python,
#    cubin, the jit-cache shim and the providers share one version (FlashInfer refuses mixed versions).
RUN python3 -c "import importlib.metadata as md, inspect, flashinfer.mla as m; from flashinfer.jit import env; from flashinfer.decode import trtllm_batch_decode_sparse_mla_dsv4 as f; assert hasattr(m, 'dsv41_fp4_quantize_pack_sparse_mla_cache'); assert 'fp8_dsv41_fp4_ca' in str(inspect.signature(f).parameters['kv_cache_format'].annotation); p = {x.provider_id: x for x in env.FLASHINFER_AOT_PROVIDERS}; assert {'sparse_mla_sm120', 'mxfp8_gemm_cutlass_sm120'} <= p['sm120f'].modules, p; v = {md.version(d).split('+')[0] for d in ('flashinfer-python', 'flashinfer-cubin', 'flashinfer-jit-cache', 'flashinfer-jit-cache-sm120f')}; assert len(v) == 1, v; print('flashinfer', *v, 'aot', sorted(p), len(p['sm120f'].modules), 'sm120f modules')" \
    && python3 -c "import torch, vllm.third_party.deep_gemm as dg; s = str(torch.ops.deep_gemm.get_theoretical_mk_alignment_for_contiguous_layout.default._schema); assert 'num_groups' in s, s; print('deep_gemm', dg.__version__, s)"

# 3. The vLLM-side patches (see header). patch_vllm_indexer_sm120.py (varlen indexer / adaptive
#    verification) stays NOT applied: measured as a net loss on 2026-09-18 and 2026-09-22.
COPY tools/dsv41_sm120/ /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/
ENV TORCH_EXTENSIONS_DIR=/opt/vllm-moet/torch_extensions
RUN python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_mxfp8_gemv.py \
    && python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_wo_a_sm120.py \
    && python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_moe_glue_sm120.py \
    && python3 -c "import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/sm120_gemv'); import mxfp8_gemv_sm120 as g; e = g._ext(); assert hasattr(e, 'mxfp8_gemv_grouped'); print('sm120 gemv extension built')" \
    && ls /opt/vllm-moet/torch_extensions/vllm_moet_mxfp8_gemv_sm120/*.so

# 4. Reasoning-effort tiers (header).
ARG VLLM_MOET_REASONING_EFFORT=1
RUN if [ "$VLLM_MOET_REASONING_EFFORT" = "1" ]; then python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_reasoning_effort.py \
    && python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/test_reasoning_effort_encoding.py; fi

# 5. nvfp4_ds_mla on sm_120 through FlashInfer's DSv4.1 dual cache + the MXFP4 indexer cache gate (header). On a
#    vLLM that writes the V4.1 records interleaved (vllm#61371) FlashInfer first learns kv_scale_placement and its
#    sparse_mla_sm120 module is rebuilt into data/aot (flashinfer_interleaved/, ~1 min).
#    VLLM_MOET_V41_KV_RECORDS names the base's placement for the image label the launcher reads (the KV offload's disk
#    tier keeps the two placements apart); the build fails if it is not what this vLLM writes.
ARG VLLM_MOET_NVFP4_KV=1
ARG VLLM_MOET_V41_KV_RECORDS=interleaved
RUN records=footer; grep -q "The V4.1 records are interleaved" /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm/models/deepseek_v41/common/ops/cache_utils.py && records=interleaved; \
    [ "$records" = "$VLLM_MOET_V41_KV_RECORDS" ] || { echo "VLLM_MOET_V41_KV_RECORDS=$VLLM_MOET_V41_KV_RECORDS but this vLLM writes $records V4.1 records" >&2; exit 1; }; \
    if [ "$VLLM_MOET_NVFP4_KV" = "1" ]; then \
      if [ "$records" = "interleaved" ]; then \
        python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/flashinfer_interleaved/patch_flashinfer_dsv41_interleaved.py --build \
        && python3 -c "import inspect; from flashinfer.decode import trtllm_batch_decode_sparse_mla_dsv4 as f; from flashinfer.jit.env import get_aot_artifacts; assert 'kv_scale_placement' in inspect.signature(f).parameters; a = get_aot_artifacts('sparse_mla_sm120'); assert a and a[0].provider_id == 'flashinfer-python', a; print('flashinfer reads interleaved V4.1 rows:', a[0].path)" \
        || exit 1; \
      fi; \
      python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_indexer_fp4_sm120.py \
      && python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/nvfp4_kv/patch_vllm_nvfp4_sm120_upstream.py; fi

# 6. Single-copy KV offload of the TP-replicated V4.1 KV (header).
ARG VLLM_MOET_OFFLOAD_DEDUP=1
RUN if [ "$VLLM_MOET_OFFLOAD_DEDUP" = "1" ]; then python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_offload_replicated_mla.py \
    && python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/test_offload_replicated_mla.py; fi

# 8. MoE input quantization + DeepGEMM grouped-layout permutation in one kernel at decode shapes (header);
#    the extension is compiled here so nothing JIT-compiles at boot. GPU tests: tools/dsv41_sm120/README.md.
RUN python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_moe_quant_scatter_sm120.py \
    && python3 -c "import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/moe_quant_scatter'); import moe_quant_scatter_sm120 as q; e = q._ext(); assert hasattr(e, 'moe_quant_scatter'); print('sm120 moe quant+scatter extension built')" \
    && ls /opt/vllm-moet/torch_extensions/vllm_moet_moe_quant_scatter_sm120/*.so

# 10. The mHC boundary off the decode critical path (header); the extension is compiled here so nothing
#     JIT-compiles at boot. GPU tests: tools/dsv41_sm120/README.md. VLLM_MOET_DSPARK_MHC_STREAM=0 leaves the
#     drafter's layers without the stream (the served wiring; an image for the KV-capacity A/B of window 9).
ARG VLLM_MOET_MHC_OVERLAP=1
ARG VLLM_MOET_DSPARK_MHC_STREAM=1
RUN if [ "$VLLM_MOET_MHC_OVERLAP" = "1" ]; then python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_mhc_overlap_sm120.py \
    && python3 -c "import vllm.models.deepseek_v41.nvidia.ops.mhc as h; assert hasattr(h, '_moet_mhc_shifted_post_pre_overlap'); print('mhc overlap patched')" \
    && if [ "$VLLM_MOET_DSPARK_MHC_STREAM" = "1" ]; then python3 /opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/patch_vllm_dspark_mhc_stream_sm120.py \
       && python3 -c "import vllm.models.deepseek_v41.nvidia.dspark as d; import inspect; s = inspect.getsource(d.DSparkDeepseekV4Model); assert 'mhc_stream=mhc_stream' in s and 'tensor_model_parallel_all_reduce(hidden_states)' in s; print('drafter mhc stream patched')"; fi \
    && python3 -c "import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/opt/vllm-moet/dsv41_sm120/mhc_overlap'); import mhc_post_norm_sm120 as m; e = m._ext(); assert hasattr(e, 'mhc_post_norm') and hasattr(e, 'mhc_proj'); print('sm120 mhc overlap extension built')" \
    && ls /opt/vllm-moet/torch_extensions/vllm_moet_mhc_post_norm_sm120/*.so; fi

# 11. The small-M BF16 GEMMs with cuBLAS's bits (header); the extension is compiled here so nothing JIT-compiles at
#     boot. GPU tests: tools/dsv41_sm120/README.md.
